# Introduction to VLSI & SoC Design

## Overview

This module provides an introduction to VLSI, ASICs, SoCs, and the basic building blocks of electronic systems.

## Topics Covered

### VLSI

- Basic meaning of VLSI
- Very Large Scale Integration
- Basic concept of integrated circuits
- Moore's Law

### MOSFET

- Basic introduction to MOSFET
- MOSFET terminals
- Source
- Gate
- Drain
- Basic meaning of channel length

### ASIC

- Basic concept of ASIC
- Application-Specific Integrated Circuit
- Application-specific hardware

### SoC

- Basic concept of System-on-Chip
- Processor
- Memory
- I/O
- Digital blocks
- Analog blocks
- Integration of multiple system functions on a chip

### Processor Concepts

- Basic introduction to ARM
- Basic introduction to RISC-V

### SoC Communication

- Basic synchronous communication
- Clock-based operation
- Parallel communication

## Key Takeaways

- Understood the basic concept of VLSI.
- Learned the basic purpose of ASICs.
- Learned the basic concept and components of an SoC.
- Understood the role of processors, memory and I/O in an electronic system.
- Received an introduction to ARM and RISC-V.
- Learned basic concepts of synchronous and parallel communication.

